   "subject": "Re: Running SEM on longitudinal data: warning message \"not all elements of the gradient are (near) zero\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Can anyone\r\nexplain what this warning message means</font></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>It means your model might not have converged on a good solution, only a &quot;local maximum&quot; (or the algorithm may have simply stopped looking because the gradient didn&#39;t point out any obvious place to look next). </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
